WEBVTT

00:01:57.770 --> 00:02:00.350
Odds or evens...?

00:02:00.860 --> 00:02:02.600
I'll go with evens.

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:07.110
Odds...

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:09.290
Oops.

00:02:09.290 --> 00:02:10.780
I lost.

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:12.760
Tragic.

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:15.460
The captain of the Harusame's 4th Squad

00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:20.070
was once considered a lone 
flower in the darkness,

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:24.140
but after losing out 
in a grab for power,

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:27.170
she stole money from the 
group and disappeared.

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:30.210
I never expected her 
to come back like this.

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:31.980
No kidding.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:35.300
I never expected you to be a 
sucker for a vixen like her.

00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:37.650
Kids wouldn't understand.

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:39.660
We live in an age where everything

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:42.100
fits in the palm of your hand.

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:45.270
But you want a woman who 
isn't so easy to hold on to.

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:46.300
Like a DS?

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:48.320
She's more like a Genesis.

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:49.820
I see.

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:52.320
No wonder it was so hard to find her.

00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:55.610
We're talking about your 
beloved Genesis here.

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:58.930
But it looks like she couldn't 
fit in down there either.

00:02:58.930 --> 00:03:01.120
She gambled and lost.

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:02.540
And so did you.

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:04.370
Hey!

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:06.290
Don't jump to conclusions.

00:03:06.630 --> 00:03:08.570
I'm not like a certain stupid captain.

00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:10.980
I don't let my emotions 
get in the way of my work.

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:11.750
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:12.890
Besides, she changed her face

00:03:12.890 --> 00:03:15.320
and name when she escaped to Earth.

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:16.710
How was I supposed to recognize her?

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:17.680
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:20.110
And I'm a Nintendo fan, not a Sega fan!

00:03:20.110 --> 00:03:21.670
You listening?!

00:03:21.670 --> 00:03:23.060
Oh well.

00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:25.470
I was interested in seeing the

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:27.230
exalted team work of the Shinra,

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:28.650
but they were just a bunch of grunts

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:30.650
who stood no chance 
one-on-one against a Yato.

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:32.430
Wouldn't be much of a fight.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:36.840
Anyway, they stole my glory again.

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:40.830
We should go show our gratitude.

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:50.380
To the samurai.

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:56.930
<b>Odds or Evens</b>

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:01.050
Shinsuke Takasugi?

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:02.740
You haven't heard of him?

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:05.400
He signed a pact with us.

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:08.150
He's the leader of the mercenary 
group known as the Kiheitai.

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:10.150
Are they from Earth?

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:12.150
They're samurai, I think.

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:13.970
The remnants of those savages

00:04:13.970 --> 00:04:15.870
who resisted until the very end

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:17.780
when we opened up their land.

00:04:19.450 --> 00:04:20.320
Admiral Assho--

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:22.380
I mean, Admiral Abo.

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:25.410
He must be very special for 
you to remember his name.

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:27.400
He only cooperates with us

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:29.140
when our interests happen to coincide,

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:31.050
but he can be very useful.

00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:36.450
You could consider them the 
Harusame's enforcers on Earth.

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:40.800
They were responsible for 
hunting down that vixen.

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:43.060
Oh, really?

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:46.060
However, there is one 
issue that concerns me.

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:47.480
I've heard that they are actually

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:49.340
a terrorist group which seeks to

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:51.560
unseat the government of Edo.

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:53.340
But when we struck a deal

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:55.070
with the central ward which

00:04:55.070 --> 00:04:57.310
allowed us to sneak into Edo,

00:04:57.310 --> 00:05:00.050
they offered to draw the 
government's trained dogs

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:01.070
away from us.

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:04.280
Do you know why?

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:06.450
That's easy.

00:05:08.270 --> 00:05:11.380
Each side is using the other,

00:05:11.380 --> 00:05:12.700
so they're using the Harusame

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:14.650
to get close to the Bakufu and

00:05:14.650 --> 00:05:16.090
take down the central ward.

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:17.950
What?! Really?!

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:21.020
I mean, you're absolutely right!

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:23.500
They're plotting terrible things!

00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:25.810
Yes, I knew all along!

00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:28.100
S-So that's how it was...

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:28.850
Damn!

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:31.940
We finally obtained the right to

00:05:31.940 --> 00:05:34.270
strip Earth of its valuable resources.

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:37.370
If they succeed, we'll lose 
all our business there.

00:05:38.260 --> 00:05:40.240
Well, I doubt that Takasugi person

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:44.500
stands a chance against 
the Tendo or the elders,

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:46.990
but he can probably crush our forces.

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:51.620
I-If that happens, the 
elders will have my hide!

00:05:52.690 --> 00:05:53.910
That's true.

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:55.410
Well, do the best you can.

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:56.980
Thanks for the food!

00:05:57.770 --> 00:05:59.730
W-Wait, Kamui!

00:05:59.730 --> 00:06:02.670
Why do you think I summoned you here?!

00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:04.520
For a free meal?

00:06:04.520 --> 00:06:05.100
No!

00:06:05.370 --> 00:06:09.850
The 7th Squad is responsible 
for cleaning up our messes!

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:13.600
So what do you want me to do?

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:17.980
Dispose of the tools 
that we no longer need.

00:06:18.890 --> 00:06:20.340
Good grief.

00:06:20.340 --> 00:06:23.240
Strong words, coming from a 
tool that never had any use but as a decoration.

00:06:23.890 --> 00:06:25.750
This place would be much more

00:06:25.750 --> 00:06:28.240
comfortable if we disposed of that pig.

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:31.180
Aren't you both four-legged creatures?

00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:33.750
Can't you get along, Captain Koro?

00:06:33.990 --> 00:06:35.130
Kamui...

00:06:35.650 --> 00:06:37.640
You have the backing of

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:39.770
the captains of the twelve squads.

00:06:39.770 --> 00:06:41.300
We're ready to throw our support

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:43.090
behind you at a moment's notice.

00:06:43.090 --> 00:06:47.370
Admiral Asshole is just 
a puppet for the elders.

00:06:47.370 --> 00:06:49.960
All he cares about is his own safety.

00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:54.230
I wanna work for someone 
who will let me run wild.

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:58.560
Then why don't you take control, Koro?

00:06:58.560 --> 00:06:59.930
I can't lead.

00:06:59.930 --> 00:07:02.360
I just want to go crazy 
and not have to think.

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:04.880
You sound just like our boss.

00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:07.750
Besides, I have an eyepatch over one eye

00:07:07.750 --> 00:07:09.500
and a hook instead of a hand.

00:07:09.500 --> 00:07:11.050
I'm not captain material.

00:07:11.050 --> 00:07:13.190
No, you're the spitting 
image of a captain.

00:07:13.190 --> 00:07:15.140
You're clearly gunning 
to be the captain.

00:07:15.140 --> 00:07:19.110
Anyway, I'm willing to lend you a hand.

00:07:19.110 --> 00:07:21.860
If you're gonna take down that 
Takasugi fool, count me in.

00:07:21.860 --> 00:07:23.420
Don't interfere.

00:07:24.090 --> 00:07:27.020
I finally found myself another samurai.

00:07:27.020 --> 00:07:30.510
Abuto, isolate Takasugi 
from his minions.

00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:33.390
Take the fleet and wipe out his men.

00:07:33.390 --> 00:07:35.840
Captain Koro, you're 
free to help out there.

00:07:36.450 --> 00:07:37.810
Here we go again...

00:07:38.700 --> 00:07:43.070
Sorry, but I won't let 
anyone ruin my fun.

00:07:47.820 --> 00:07:49.910
I can't stand space.

00:07:50.520 --> 00:07:52.340
It's so dark everywhere.

00:07:52.670 --> 00:07:57.420
Can't tell if we're moving 
forward or backward.

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:02.170
Lord Shinsuke, are we 
moving forward right now?

00:08:03.190 --> 00:08:05.280
Sorry about sounding so whiny.

00:08:05.770 --> 00:08:07.930
I've been getting worried.

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:10.570
Doesn't matter which way we're going.

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:13.310
If you get lost,

00:08:13.310 --> 00:08:14.930
just follow my lead.

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:18.820
Whether you're deep underground 
or far above the clouds,

00:08:18.820 --> 00:08:21.690
I promise to take you to our goal.

00:08:22.040 --> 00:08:23.610
There's no need to worry

00:08:23.610 --> 00:08:25.510
as long as you believe in me.

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:27.960
L-Lord Shinsuke!

00:08:27.960 --> 00:08:30.700
I...  I'll follow you to hell and back!

00:08:30.700 --> 00:08:32.800
We share the same goal.

00:08:33.310 --> 00:08:35.080
Let us march on.

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:37.310
Now sign this petition.

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:39.720
We oppose the

00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:43.350
Greater Edo Ordinance Regarding 
the Healthy Development of Youths!

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:45.000
Before you try to regulate free speech,

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:47.040
you should learn to 
regulate your own heart!

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:50.150
Pedophilia predates manga and anime!

00:08:50.150 --> 00:08:53.310
Is it not our goal to foster 
a culture of acceptance?!

00:08:53.310 --> 00:08:56.180
Incidentally, I'm not a 
pedophile.  I'm a feminist.

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:01.860
Bansai-senpai.

00:09:01.860 --> 00:09:03.120
Where's Lord Shinsuke?

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:04.770
He stayed behind on the mothership

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:06.910
because the admiral needed 
him for something.

00:09:06.910 --> 00:09:09.070
We're supposed to return 
to Edo without him.

00:09:09.330 --> 00:09:10.610
Needed him for what?

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:13.620
Well, I haven't the slightest idea.

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:16.560
I have a bad feeling about this.

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:20.000
Was it a mistake to join 
forces with the Harusame?

00:09:20.680 --> 00:09:22.400
Why are you saying this now?

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:26.530
We will defeat the Bakufu 
and rebuild the world.

00:09:26.530 --> 00:09:28.510
Didn't you agree to the plan?

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:31.490
But we're out of our league...

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:36.400
The Kiheitai aren't 
on the same level as a

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:38.480
galactic crime syndicate.

00:09:38.830 --> 00:09:41.920
Soon enough, we'll become their pawns.

00:09:42.590 --> 00:09:44.150
The way things stand,

00:09:44.150 --> 00:09:46.250
we've sunken to the level of the

00:09:46.250 --> 00:09:48.030
Amanto-ass-kissing Bakufu.

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:51.100
Besides, now that the 
Bakufu and Harusame

00:09:51.100 --> 00:09:52.570
are working together,

00:09:52.570 --> 00:09:55.530
we've become a liability.

00:09:56.600 --> 00:09:58.540
What if Lord Shinsuke is...

00:09:59.190 --> 00:10:02.680
So in other words, you're 
worried about Shinsuke?

00:10:02.680 --> 00:10:04.400
Don't worry.

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:07.060
That man won't fall 
before the Bakufu does.

00:10:07.060 --> 00:10:08.950
Did you forget the promise he made?

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:13.390
I'll simply destroy...

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:18.890
...the Greater Edo Ordinance Regarding 
the Healthy Development of Youths!

00:10:18.890 --> 00:10:20.920
Don't mess up my memories!

00:10:20.920 --> 00:10:21.740
Die!

00:10:21.740 --> 00:10:22.810
We'll destroy you first!

00:10:23.130 --> 00:10:24.330
Master Bansai!

00:10:24.330 --> 00:10:26.820
There's a Harusame fleet ahead of us!

00:10:27.450 --> 00:10:30.080
What? Do they truly 
intend to eliminate us?!

00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:33.720
L-Lord Shinsuke!

00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:35.480
Hey.

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:36.410
So we meet again.

00:10:38.290 --> 00:10:40.490
Sorry about cutting 
straight to the chase,

00:10:40.490 --> 00:10:43.220
but either way, you're going to 
be surprised when I say this.

00:10:43.710 --> 00:10:44.790
Please die.

00:10:45.190 --> 00:10:47.620
That's not much of a surprise.

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:50.800
It was obvious from the 
moment I first saw you.

00:10:51.270 --> 00:10:53.390
You're sharp.

00:10:53.390 --> 00:10:56.180
You see, I've been dying 
to fight a samurai

00:10:56.180 --> 00:10:58.560
from the moment I first saw one.

00:10:59.090 --> 00:11:01.780
And you kind of smell the same

00:11:01.780 --> 00:11:04.190
as that other samurai.

00:11:04.190 --> 00:11:05.670
What a coincidence.

00:11:05.670 --> 00:11:08.180
I've been dying to kill 
that stupid samurai

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:09.690
with the silver hair.

00:11:11.070 --> 00:11:14.700
You must have super powers or something.

00:11:15.350 --> 00:11:17.670
Is there a secret behind 
that left eye of yours?

00:11:18.460 --> 00:11:19.430
Kamui!

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:25.120
I told you not to interfere.

00:11:26.020 --> 00:11:27.420
I won't interfere.

00:11:33.120 --> 00:11:33.630
Huh?

00:11:33.990 --> 00:11:37.510
Kamui, we're here to kill you.

00:11:41.450 --> 00:11:43.850
Did I miss a message or something?

00:11:44.250 --> 00:11:45.960
Nobody ever mentioned that

00:11:45.960 --> 00:11:47.860
we were up against such a big family.

00:11:48.390 --> 00:11:50.610
You Yato are too dangerous.

00:11:51.070 --> 00:11:54.610
A blade that's too sharp will 
attract many foes, Kamui.

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:56.590
You got me good.

00:11:56.590 --> 00:11:58.960
Never expected Admiral Asshole 
to pull a fast one on me.

00:11:58.960 --> 00:12:01.820
I'll kill that idiot for you.

00:12:01.820 --> 00:12:05.130
So feel free to rest in peace.

00:12:13.220 --> 00:12:14.210
Vice-captain!

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:17.060
There's a Harusame fleet 
behind the Kiheitai!

00:12:17.060 --> 00:12:19.600
It's Captain Koro's 8th Squad,

00:12:19.600 --> 00:12:22.180
along with the admiral's personal fleet!

00:12:24.480 --> 00:12:27.390
Looks like we were tricked.

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:31.110
Wh-What's going on?

00:12:31.540 --> 00:12:33.680
The Harusame are fighting each other?

00:12:33.680 --> 00:12:36.470
There's no need to worry, folks.

00:12:36.470 --> 00:12:38.490
Everything is going according to plan.

00:12:38.490 --> 00:12:39.620
Takechi-senpai...

00:12:40.290 --> 00:12:42.340
That is the Harusame's 7th Squad.

00:12:42.340 --> 00:12:44.510
The strongest Harusame force, drawn from

00:12:44.510 --> 00:12:46.660
the elite ranks of the 
Yato, the warrior tribe.

00:12:47.130 --> 00:12:50.130
Their leader, the brilliant Lord Kamui,

00:12:50.130 --> 00:12:54.460
is more highly regarded 
than the admiral now.

00:12:54.460 --> 00:12:57.260
The 12 squad captains are looking 
to overthrow the admiral

00:12:57.260 --> 00:13:00.180
and name Lord Kamui as their leader.

00:13:00.410 --> 00:13:02.880
So by that reasoning,

00:13:02.890 --> 00:13:04.550
that fool of an admiral

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:07.010
intends to eliminate the 7th Squad,

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:09.190
which threatens his position?

00:13:09.190 --> 00:13:11.240
Exactly.

00:13:11.240 --> 00:13:16.450
We were used as bait to isolate 
and crush the 7th Squad,

00:13:16.450 --> 00:13:18.700
the strongest of them all.

00:13:19.020 --> 00:13:22.160
So we're being used 
by the Harusame again?

00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:25.470
It's easier for us to take advantage

00:13:25.470 --> 00:13:28.100
of that useless admiral.

00:13:29.590 --> 00:13:31.100
But still...

00:13:31.100 --> 00:13:33.670
Destroying your own fangs to 
hold onto your position...

00:13:34.250 --> 00:13:35.930
There are always more fools

00:13:35.930 --> 00:13:39.080
when an organization begins to grow.

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:43.270
Friend Takasugi, that 
was an excellent job!

00:13:43.270 --> 00:13:46.600
There are no longer any 
rogue elements to oppose me!

00:13:46.600 --> 00:13:49.560
You also performed admirably, Koro.

00:13:49.830 --> 00:13:52.150
No, Admiral Assho...

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:53.870
Admiral Abo.

00:13:53.870 --> 00:13:55.320
I was simply performing 
my duty as one of

00:13:55.320 --> 00:13:56.570
the 12 squad captains.

00:13:57.060 --> 00:13:59.160
Now that Kamui has been 
made an example of,

00:13:59.160 --> 00:14:01.760
the captains who supported 
Kamui will come

00:14:01.760 --> 00:14:04.530
to their senses and swear fealty to you.

00:14:04.530 --> 00:14:06.540
It was kind of a waste.

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:08.080
Hm?

00:14:08.730 --> 00:14:11.710
That kid took enough poison to

00:14:11.710 --> 00:14:13.420
instantly leave an 
elephant incapacitated,

00:14:14.130 --> 00:14:16.040
but he was able to fend off my blade

00:14:16.040 --> 00:14:18.550
while smiling the entire time.

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:20.660
And he managed to kill off

00:14:20.660 --> 00:14:23.700
twenty or so of your men, 
despite his injuries.

00:14:24.430 --> 00:14:27.010
I have a feeling that his absence

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:28.890
will be far more damaging

00:14:28.890 --> 00:14:30.560
than what he did to your men.

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:32.070
It doesn't matter.

00:14:32.070 --> 00:14:35.440
Your Kiheitai can fill the 
void he's left behind.

00:14:36.570 --> 00:14:38.690
Sorry, but I'll pass.

00:14:39.150 --> 00:14:42.100
It's better to be the head of 
a cat than the tail of a lion.

00:14:42.530 --> 00:14:46.780
I'd rather be a bandit chief 
than a pirate or bigwig.

00:14:47.520 --> 00:14:52.080
Besides, I'm not giving 
up the Kiheitai name.

00:14:52.440 --> 00:14:54.150
Allow me to compensate you...

00:14:54.150 --> 00:14:55.580
I don't need anything.

00:14:55.580 --> 00:14:59.590
Let's keep it simple, just like before.

00:14:59.940 --> 00:15:01.580
Be careful.

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:05.590
He's harder to read than Kamui was.

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:07.400
I know.

00:15:07.400 --> 00:15:09.100
No more fooling around.

00:15:11.100 --> 00:15:16.230
Odds or evens, odds or evens...?

00:15:17.650 --> 00:15:18.610
Odds.

00:15:21.370 --> 00:15:22.790
Too bad...

00:15:22.790 --> 00:15:24.180
Evens...

00:15:24.180 --> 00:15:27.120
Oops, now it's your turn to die.

00:15:27.740 --> 00:15:29.690
That gambler's cursed.

00:15:29.690 --> 00:15:32.120
If you lose, you run out of luck.

00:15:32.570 --> 00:15:34.620
I lost, so I know what 
I'm talking about.

00:15:36.870 --> 00:15:40.130
Coming from a monster who 
doesn't die when killed...

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:43.090
They patched me up and spared my life

00:15:43.090 --> 00:15:47.220
so I could be executed in 
front of the others, right?

00:15:47.220 --> 00:15:48.380
When's the big day?

00:15:48.380 --> 00:15:49.640
In three days.

00:15:49.640 --> 00:15:51.110
Three days...

00:15:51.110 --> 00:15:53.640
I wonder which one of us will die first.

00:15:54.070 --> 00:15:56.080
I'm sure you've figured it out already.

00:15:56.730 --> 00:16:00.650
The people here only 
care about themselves.

00:16:01.010 --> 00:16:02.870
Doesn't matter how hard you work.

00:16:02.870 --> 00:16:04.900
They'll just abuse you 
as much as they can

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:06.390
before they get rid of you.

00:16:06.390 --> 00:16:07.610
True.

00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:10.640
I would prefer to be used by someone

00:16:10.640 --> 00:16:13.530
who isn't so pathetic.

00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:19.860
Those sharp fangs of yours 
will only rot in this place.

00:16:21.240 --> 00:16:24.050
Why did you come here?

00:16:25.160 --> 00:16:26.980
I'm the same as you.

00:16:27.390 --> 00:16:33.310
Searching for a place to 
use my sharpened fangs.

00:16:34.240 --> 00:16:38.310
But this leaky boat 
won't take me anywhere.

00:16:38.920 --> 00:16:44.040
I'd rather hitch a ride on your ship.

00:16:45.580 --> 00:16:48.570
See ya, space fighter.

00:16:50.010 --> 00:16:53.300
I don't see how the admiral 
took out the 7th Squad...

00:16:53.300 --> 00:16:55.460
Did he have help from the elders?

00:16:55.460 --> 00:16:59.390
No, I heard that the idea came 
from Takasugi of the Kiheitai.

00:16:59.390 --> 00:17:01.280
It's a sad story.

00:17:01.280 --> 00:17:04.660
Those guys worked their 
asses off for the Harusame.

00:17:04.660 --> 00:17:08.350
Nobody's doing jack for 
the sake of the Harusame.

00:17:08.640 --> 00:17:11.320
If someone is in the 
way, you eliminate them.

00:17:11.320 --> 00:17:13.430
That's how it goes in the Harusame.

00:17:15.170 --> 00:17:17.430
Men, take a long, hard look!

00:17:18.030 --> 00:17:20.460
This is what happens to 
those who defy my authority!

00:17:20.460 --> 00:17:22.760
When you cross me, you cross the elders!

00:17:22.760 --> 00:17:26.190
When you cross the elders, 
you cross the Harusame!

00:17:26.550 --> 00:17:28.710
When there is no order,

00:17:28.710 --> 00:17:32.000
a battle-hardened army will 
be reduced to a headless mob!

00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:33.700
How can he say that crap 
with a straight face?

00:17:34.190 --> 00:17:37.450
Kamui, do you have any last words?

00:17:37.830 --> 00:17:39.850
Can I say something real quick?

00:17:39.850 --> 00:17:41.120
Yes.

00:17:41.760 --> 00:17:42.960
Admiral Asshole!

00:17:43.130 --> 00:17:44.960
Kill him! Kill him now!

00:17:45.420 --> 00:17:47.030
Hold on, Admiral Assho--

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:48.860
Admiral Abo.

00:17:49.310 --> 00:17:51.710
Will you allow me to kill him?

00:17:51.710 --> 00:17:52.390
Huh?

00:17:52.660 --> 00:17:57.050
Unfortunately, I never had the 
chance to fight him one-on-one,

00:17:57.050 --> 00:17:59.390
but I can at least serve 
as the executioner.

00:17:59.630 --> 00:18:02.900
On my signal, jump Takasugi.

00:18:05.370 --> 00:18:11.460
Our luck ran out when I 
got on this leaky boat.

00:18:12.210 --> 00:18:16.410
You're saying that we share 
the same fight, Earth fighter?

00:18:16.920 --> 00:18:17.940
Who knows?

00:18:18.460 --> 00:18:21.420
All I know is that neither of us 
will be doing any sightseeing.

00:18:22.620 --> 00:18:24.040
Sure we will.

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:25.460
Down in hell.

00:18:27.520 --> 00:18:28.420
You bet.

00:18:40.880 --> 00:18:43.400
Have a nice nap in hell,

00:18:43.800 --> 00:18:46.190
leaky boat crew.

00:18:59.990 --> 00:19:02.710
Wh-What?!

00:19:03.160 --> 00:19:04.810
I told you so.

00:19:04.810 --> 00:19:06.960
That gambler's cursed.

00:19:06.960 --> 00:19:09.420
I wanted to see which one 
of us would die first,

00:19:09.420 --> 00:19:11.220
but you're trying to 
get us killed together?

00:19:11.880 --> 00:19:13.970
It's more fun to dance

00:19:13.970 --> 00:19:18.220
with a batshit crazy idiot 
than a plain old idiot.

00:19:21.060 --> 00:19:23.980
Samurai are a blast.

00:19:24.180 --> 00:19:25.470
Takasugi!

00:19:25.470 --> 00:19:27.630
You're nothing more than tools 
that are no longer needed!

00:19:27.630 --> 00:19:29.980
I'll turn you into spacedust!

00:19:30.710 --> 00:19:32.990
You're the one who's no longer needed.

00:19:33.360 --> 00:19:34.790
Didn't you hear me?

00:19:34.790 --> 00:19:37.150
I'm the executioner here,

00:19:37.150 --> 00:19:41.500
the only executioner 
needed in this place.

00:19:42.920 --> 00:19:45.310
Off with your heads.

00:19:51.740 --> 00:19:53.310
Lord Shinsuke!

00:19:53.310 --> 00:19:55.260
This is how the Joi do it!

00:19:55.260 --> 00:19:57.180
I'll follow you to hell and back!

00:19:58.550 --> 00:20:00.090
Are you insane?!

00:20:00.090 --> 00:20:02.760
You believe that we stand a 
chance against the Harusame?

00:20:02.760 --> 00:20:04.490
We should be focusing our resources

00:20:04.490 --> 00:20:06.560
on the Greater Edo Ordinance Reg...

00:20:07.730 --> 00:20:09.900
You'd have to be insane...

00:20:10.260 --> 00:20:13.440
...to pick a fight with 
the rest of the world!

00:20:13.710 --> 00:20:15.450
Accursed monkeys!

00:20:15.450 --> 00:20:16.650
What are you doing?!

00:20:16.650 --> 00:20:18.150
Crush them!

00:20:18.930 --> 00:20:19.580
What?!

00:20:21.920 --> 00:20:23.050
Oh?

00:20:23.050 --> 00:20:26.490
I rowed out here because I was worried,

00:20:26.490 --> 00:20:28.870
but you're looking better than usual.

00:20:28.870 --> 00:20:30.210
Blockhead.

00:20:30.480 --> 00:20:31.710
The 7th Squad!

00:20:31.710 --> 00:20:32.560
Impossible!

00:20:32.560 --> 00:20:34.210
Why are they alive?!

00:20:34.510 --> 00:20:35.720
Admiral!

00:20:35.720 --> 00:20:36.700
Bad news!

00:20:36.700 --> 00:20:38.590
Now that the 7th Squad is back,

00:20:38.580 --> 00:20:41.820
the other squads are beginning 
to side with them!

00:20:41.820 --> 00:20:44.140
Th-The tables have been reversed.

00:20:44.140 --> 00:20:44.730
Huh?

00:20:44.940 --> 00:20:46.230
Admiral!

00:20:47.270 --> 00:20:49.690
C-Curse you, Kamui, Takasugi!

00:20:49.700 --> 00:20:50.590
You won't get away with this!

00:20:50.590 --> 00:20:51.650
A-Admiral!

00:20:51.650 --> 00:20:53.340
Why are you running away by yourself?!

00:20:53.340 --> 00:20:55.650
Take me with you, Admiral Asshole!

00:20:55.650 --> 00:20:57.240
Ah! You finally said it!

00:20:57.250 --> 00:21:00.180
I kept pretending that I didn't hear 
you, but you finally said it to my face!

00:21:00.180 --> 00:21:01.870
You're a dead man!

00:21:01.870 --> 00:21:03.150
Get this ship moving!

00:21:03.150 --> 00:21:04.410
What are you doing?!

00:21:04.410 --> 00:21:05.460
Shut up!

00:21:05.460 --> 00:21:07.920
My men always do the work, 
so I have no idea what to do!

00:21:07.920 --> 00:21:09.460
Don't you have a hook on your hand?!

00:21:09.460 --> 00:21:10.630
You're supposed to be a captain!

00:21:10.630 --> 00:21:12.080
You're supposed to be an admiral!

00:21:12.080 --> 00:21:12.520
Huh?

00:21:12.520 --> 00:21:13.220
H-Hey!

00:21:13.220 --> 00:21:14.000
What's that?!

00:21:15.010 --> 00:21:16.690
Ka-Kamui!

00:21:16.690 --> 00:21:19.470
It's not Kamui, Admiral Asshole.

00:21:19.470 --> 00:21:20.750
Starting today,

00:21:20.750 --> 00:21:21.890
I'm Admiral Nincompoop.

00:21:29.000 --> 00:21:31.020
I owe you big now.

00:21:31.520 --> 00:21:32.690
Oh well.

00:21:32.690 --> 00:21:35.610
Guess I'll have to put off 
our fight for a while.

00:21:35.610 --> 00:21:38.530
Besides, I'm looking forward 
to touring hell with you.

00:21:39.750 --> 00:21:42.530
Now, where do we start?

00:21:42.910 --> 00:21:45.510
I'm guessing the planet of samurai?

00:21:47.290 --> 00:21:52.000
Odds or evens, odds or evens...?

00:21:54.450 --> 00:21:55.550
Evens.

00:21:56.570 --> 00:21:58.300
Too bad...

00:21:58.300 --> 00:21:59.940
Odds...

00:23:40.070 --> 00:23:45.070
<b>Next Episode
I Can't Remember a Damn Thing About the Factory Tour</b>

00:23:40.820 --> 00:23:41.630
Next time:

00:23:41.630 --> 00:23:45.070
I can't remember a damn thing 
about the factory tour.
